  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Audiences, organisers and students pay for quality and reliability. They judge you by performance, reputation and professionalism.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is practising daily and recording your progress.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and music, dance and performing arts careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can generate music and visuals and help with editing. Routine production work shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Live presence, taste and trust hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and edit; later, perform and teach with your own voice.
  </p>

